SPANISH 5
&
\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
%
% RULE RActive
< m1:I1::VERBPPROP{VERBPPROPrec1}
                           [ I4:mu1,
                             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                                    [head/I2::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu3],
                                     mu2
                                    ],
                             mu4
                           ]
>

< m :I3::VERBPPROP{VERBPPROPrec2}
                           [ I4:mu1,
                             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                                    [head/I2::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu3],
                                     mu2
                                    ],
                             mu4 
                           ]
>


   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: VERBPPROPrec1.voice = omegavoice
       I2: VERBrec1.modo = omegamodo
       I3: VERBPPROPrec2.voice = Active
       I4: NOT EXIST (mu1, [subjrel/EMPTYVAR{EMPTYVARrec1}])
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: Active IN VERBrec1.possvoices
          A1: VERBPPROPrec2 := VERBPPROPrec1;
              VERBPPROPrec2.voice := Active
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* name:] RActive
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] Verbppropformation
\item[* class:] RC: VoiceRules
\item[* date of creation:] 02-FEBR-1988 11:00:00  
\item[* author:] Elly van Munster, Lisette Appelo
\item[* copied from:] Jan Odijk
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 31/1/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster\\
Mu4 added for efficiency reasons, in order to block candidates for a 
{\bf SE}active rule already in this RC. \\
(Otherwise the derivation would be blocked in EMPTYsustitution,
since ther is a condition on voice = {\bf SE}active.)
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To generate Active voice structures.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:] Introduction of a Voice-parameter, in which
case the information can be maintained in which voice (active or passive) the 
Dutch sentence was put.\\ 
Now all voicerules apply in principle. Only the conditions on the rules
and the model-specifications  avoid certain applications.
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:] dna
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[* relevant examples:] Juan lee un libro, Llega Juan, etc..
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{verbatim}
The IL-mapping is as follows:
IL-active   ----->>   Sp.1) active 
                         2) SEactive 

IL-passive  ----->>   Sp.1) SEpassive
                         2) SEactive
                         3) active
                         4) passive
\end{verbatim}
\end{description}

\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RSEactive1
< m1:I1::VERBPPROP{VERBPPROPrec1}
                           [ mu6,
                             subjrel/EMPTYVAR{EMPTYVARrec1},
                             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                                    [ head/I2::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu2],
                                      mu1
                                    ],
                             mu3
                           ]
>

< m :I3::VERBPPROP{VERBPPROPrec2}
                           [ mu6,
                             subjrel/EMPTYVAR{EMPTYVARrec1},
                             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                                    [ head/I2::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu2],
                                      mu1
                                    ],
                             mu3
                           ]
>


   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: VERBPPROPrec1.voice = omegavoice
       I2: (VERBrec1.modo = omegamodo) AND
           (VERBrec1.reflexivity = notreflexive)
       I3: VERBPPROPrec2.voice = SEactive
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: (Active IN VERBrec1.possvoices) AND
              (VERBrec1.thetavp = vp100)
          A1: VERBPPROPrec2 := VERBPPROPrec1;
              VERBPPROPrec2.voice := SEactive
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
