\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RSEpassive
< m1:I1::VERBPPROP{VERBPPROPrec1}
                      [ I6:mu6,
                        subjrel/EMPTYVAR{EMPTYVARrec1},
                        I7:mu1,
                        predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                               [ head/I2::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu3],
                                 mu4,
                                 objrel/T1,
                                 mu2
                               ],
                        mu5
                      ]
>

< m :I3::VERBPPROP{VERBPPROPrec2}
                      [ I6:mu6,
                        I7:mu1,
                        predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                               [ head/I4::VERB{VERBrec2}[mu3],
                                 mu4,
                                 objrel/T1,
                                 porobjrel/VARPREPP{VARPREPPrec1}
                                     [ head/PREP(KEY_doorporprepkey){PREPrec1},
                                       objrel/EMPTYVAR{EMPTYVARrec1}
                                     ],
                                 mu2
                               ],
                        mu5
                      ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: ( VERBPPROPrec1.voice = omegavoice) AND
           ( VERBPPROPrec1.thetavp IN [vp120, vp123] )  
       I2: (VERBrec1.modo = omegamodo) AND
           (VERBrec1.reflexivity = notreflexive)
       I3: ( VERBPPROPrec2.voice = SEpassive) AND
           ( VERBPPROPrec2.thetavp IN [vp120, vp123] )
       I4: VERBrec2.modo = omegamodo
       I6: ALL(mu6, leftdislocrel/..)
       I7: NOT EXIST(mu1, [leftdislocrel/..])
      >

<
   SUBRULE (*a*)
      <T1: NPVAR{NPVARrec1} >
      <T1: NPVAR{NPVARrec1} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: ((NPVARrec1.human = NoHuman
               ) OR
               (NPVARrec1.human = OmegaHuman AND
                NPVARrec1.NPhead <> persproNP
               ) OR
               (NPVARrec1.human = OmegaHuman AND
                NPVARrec1.NPhead = persproNP AND
                NPVARrec1.genero = neutro
               )
              ) OR
              (NPVARrec1.generic = yesgeneric)
            C2: Passive IN VERBrec1.possvoices
            A2: VERBrec2 := VERBrec1;
                VERBPPROPrec2 := VERBPPROPrec1;
                VERBPPROPrec2.voice := SEpassive;

                VARPREPPrec1 :=
                {
                 actsubcefs  : [doorpor]
                 headkey     : KEY_doorporprepkey
                 synppefs    : [synEMPTY]
                }
            (* all other attributes keep the default value *)

          A1:  @
         >
   SUBRULE (*b*)
      <T1: CNVAR{CNVARrec1} >
      <T1: CNVAR{CNVARrec1} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: (CNVARrec1.human = NoHuman) OR
              (CNVARrec1.human = OmegaHuman)
              
               (* CNVAR has no attribute "generic" ! *)

            C2: Passive IN VERBrec1.possvoices
            A2: VERBrec2 := VERBrec1;
                VERBPPROPrec2 := VERBPPROPrec1;
                VERBPPROPrec2.voice := SEpassive;

                VARPREPPrec1 :=
                {
                 actsubcefs  : [doorpor]
                 headkey     : KEY_doorporprepkey
                 synppefs    : [synEMPTY]
                }
            (* all other attributes keep the default value *)

          A1:  @
         >
>
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* name:] RSEpassive
\item[* kind of rule:] M-Rule
\item[* subgrammar:] Verbppropformation
\item[* class:] RC: Voice Rules
\item[* date of creation:] 02-FEBR-1988 13:40:00
\item[* author:] Elly van Munster, Lisette Appelo
\item[* copied from:] Jan Odijk
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 11/03/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster\\
Added a subrule for CNVAR.
\item date: 31/1/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster\\
Condition on Animate changed into a condition on Human.\\
(in order to allow: "Se pegan los bueyes")
\item date: 22/03/90\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo\\
Conditions on omegahuman and perspro added to avoid * "se nos vendemos" and
allow "se vende (ello)", "se venden estos" etc., because they can have a non-
human interpretation.
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To form structures in passive Voice (with SE). This is only 
possible if there is a -human DO (without the prep. {\em a}!!).
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
The splitting up for NPVAR and CNVAR is necessary since CNVAR doens't have the 
attribute "generic".
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification 
of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
